        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "acc5b48250297fd183709c9edd51fa37180b8f54983eb6d542e73602dd6ffa14",
        "target": "Given:\n- Sewers capacity: 240,000 gallons\n- Runoff per hour of rain: 1000 gallons\n\nTo find:\n- Number of days of rain the sewers can handle\n\nFirst, calculate the number of hours of rain the sewers can handle:\n\\[ \\text{Hours of rain} = \\frac{\\text{Sewers capacity}}{\\text{Runoff per hour}} = \\frac{240,000 \\text{ gallons}}{1000 \\text{ gallons/hour}} = 240 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nNext, convert hours to days:\n\\[ \\text{Days of rain} = \\frac{\\text{Hours of rain}}{24 \\text{ hours/day}} = \\frac{240 \\text{ hours}}{24 \\text{ hours/day}} = 10 \\text{ days} \\]\n\nSo, the sewers can handle 10 days of rain before they overflow.\n\nFINAL: 10",
